  "rule": "(2 if weight >= neighbor_cover else 0) + (weight + residual_pack - 0.2*max(0,residual_cover-residual_pack) - neighbor_pack/(1+boundary_edges/(1+degree)))/max(1e-9,weight+conflict_weight+compatible_weight) + 0.001*weight/max(1e-9,weight+conflict_weight)",
  "rationale": "The identical parents share residual packing and covering estimates, neighbor opportunity cost, and boundary structure. This variant prioritizes certified exchanges: a root whose weight reaches the clique-cover bound on its active neighbors can replace any selected independent subset of those neighbors without losing weight. Remaining ranking favors attainable residual reward, penalizes cover-pack uncertainty, and uses boundary edges to discount neighbor cost with diminishing returns instead of adding an unrestricted bonus. Every structural set is restricted to available vertices."
